  "note": "Span-lock: the gate decides only WHERE a value starts; once open, tape.tok_ids is emitted verbatim and neither the gate nor the LM is consulted until the span ends. Training stays a soft mixture (257: hard-commit-only training collapses the stop gate); --train-mode open additionally withholds gradient from the gate on in-span steps, which is the signal that taught it to defer to a confident LM mid-word. G_span_verbatim is an assertion, not a score: an opened span is bit-identical to the slot, so the weights contribute exactly nothing to the value. G_length_flat and G_prior_invariant are the scaling claims -- under the lock, EM must stop depending on value length or on whether the LM can spell it.",
